The error messages name neither the method nor the path.

lib/WWW/MetaForge/ArcRaiders.pm:254-257 and lib/WWW/MetaForge/GameMapData.pm:183-186 croak with sprintf("API request failed: %s %s", $response->code, $response->message). The url stands only in the debug log (:248).

Failure case: "metaforge-arcraiders map nonexistent" answers "API request failed: 400 Bad Request". The user does not see which endpoint and which parameter went wrong.

Decide: the croak message names the method and the path as well.

